# Union-merge for the brain-owned durable record log (ADR-0017, REQ-MF-3,
# issue #214/C1b). This uses git's BUILT-IN `union`
# merge driver — no per-clone `git config` registration required.
#
# NO LONGER LOAD-BEARING (issue #677). A merge driver — built-in or not — is a
# LOCAL git mechanism, and the merge that lands work in this repository is the
# forge's merge button, which does not apply it. So the strategy the durable log
# leaned on was absent at exactly the moment it was needed: the first
# memory-capturing PR merged clean and every subsequent one conflicted, on the
# one file where a hand-resolution drops a record silently.
#
# `.memory/records/` now holds ONE RECORD PER FILE (`<yyyy-mm>-<id>.jsonl`), so
# two different records are two different paths and there is nothing to union.
# Measured driver-free on the same two records and the same base: one month file
# → CONFLICT; one file each → clean, both records present.
#
# The line stays because where the driver DOES run it still turns the one
# residual case — the same `id` written with divergent bytes (ADR-0017
# Amendment 1) — into a two-line file the reindex deduplicates and reports,
# instead of a conflict. It is now a convenience, not the mechanism the format
# depends on. Nothing here may be cited as making the log conflict-free again.
/.memory/records/*.jsonl merge=union
